<title>USA: U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. rice major sales activity in the week ended Oct 3 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p>Net Sales:	1996/97		 1997/98</p>
<p> South Africa   13,100		   Nil</p>
<p> Mexico	   12,500-A</p>
<p> Turkey	   12,500</p>
<p> Netherlands    11,100</p>
<p> Ghana	     4,000</p>
<p> Trinidad	  3,800-B</p>
<p> Congo	     3,200</p>
<p> Peru		1,100-C</p>
<p>A-includes 12,100 rough rice.</p>
<p>B- all rough</p>
<p>C- all rough</p>
<p>Exports of 66,700 tonnes were up one percent from the previous week and 45 percent above the four-week average.</p>
<p>Primary export destinations: Netherlands (13,500), Mexico (13,200), Peru (13,100), Saudi Arabia (10,000) and Ghana (7,300)</p>
</text>
